<task id="017" project="field-mapping-server-write-path-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Re-point the child-records route, chat create / email.draft / budget inquiry and decision cores at RecordCreationService (FR-13 part 1)</title>
    <phase>2 W2 Unified RecordCreationService</phase>
    <gate>016 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .cs in Sprk.Bff.Api; tags include bff-api, ai-tools, security; removes the create half of a security-critical core (OwnedChildWrite); adds tests at KEEP paths (TEST-MODIFYING override).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Four callers with different principals and different error contracts move onto one service; mistakes silently weaken authorization.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits ChildRecordEndpoints.cs and OwnedChildWrite.cs (hot files, UAC-r2 PR #2110) and ontology-r1-owned decision cores; also sequences the DI swap with 018.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>016</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, ai-tools, security, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>10-14 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Re-point these callers at `RecordCreationService` (caller principal): the child-records route create (`Api/ChildRecordEndpoints.cs` ~:258), the chat `dataverse.create_record` handler (`DataverseCreateRecordHandler.cs` ~:341), `email.draft` (`EmailDraftToolHandler.cs` ~:455) and the budget inquiry executor (`BudgetInquiryExecutor.cs` ~:242). The decision route cores reach the service through `DecisionRouteCores.CreateChildAsync` -> `ChildRecordEndpoints.CreateAsync`; verify, with a test, that they inherit the service rather than re-pointing them separately. Remove the create half of `OwnedChildWrite` (keep `RefileAsync` and anything the re-file path or other non-create callers still use). Chat-created children then carry the I-1 stamp, I-16 and sharee mirror at create.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, .NET 10 BFF, Dataverse write-path security. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>The route, chat create, email.draft, budget inquiry and decision follow-on creates all go through `RecordCreationService`; `OwnedChildWrite` no longer has a create path; route-level filters, the route ledger and every caller's response contract are unchanged except for the new warnings; a chat-created child carries its I-1 stamp at create.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec.md FR-13 (part 1), FR-12, NFR-07, NFR-08. Today four callers call `OwnedChildWrite.CreateAsync` (grep result: ChildRecordEndpoints.cs ~:258, DataverseCreateRecordHandler.cs ~:341, EmailDraftToolHandler.cs ~:455, BudgetInquiryExecutor.cs ~:242). The decision follow-ons (`AddTodoExecutor`, `AssignWorkExecutor` in `Services/Signals/Actions/DecisionActionExecutors.cs`, base `ChildCreateExecutorBase` ~:1015) create through `DecisionRouteCores.CreateChildAsync` (`Services/Signals/Actions/DecisionRouteCores.cs` ~:74) which calls `ChildRecordEndpoints.CreateAsync`. ontology-r1 owns the decision cores: change only the call that reaches the create. Route-level authorization (filters, `RequireAuthorization`, the RouteAuthorizationGuardTests ledger) stays as is (ADR-008). The chat tools run as the user (user-OBO) but create app-only, so they use the caller principal.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ChildRecordEndpoints.cs (CreateAsync ~:224-258; CreateTables ~:66 unchanged here, widened in task 020)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Handlers/DataverseCreateRecordHandler.cs (~:341; also uses OwnedChildWrite.ForPersonColumns ~:496 and WhoAmI ~:502, which move into the service)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Handlers/EmailDraftToolHandler.cs (~:455)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/Actions/BudgetInquiryExecutor.cs (~:242)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/Actions/DecisionRouteCores.cs (CreateChildAsync ~:74; only if it still depends on a removed OwnedChildWrite create symbol)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/OwnedChildWrite.cs (remove create half; keep RefileAsync ~:1497 and symbols still referenced by CommunicationEndpoints.cs, EventEndpoints.cs, DataverseUpdateRecordHandler.cs, GridOverviewHandler.cs, SecureRootInheritance.cs, SignalReadService.cs, SignalSuppressionService.cs)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/RecordCreation/RecordCreationService.cs (tasks 013-016)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/RecordCreation/RecordCreationProblemMap.cs (shared refusal map, task 013)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/data-mutation/RecordOwnership/SecureChildOwnershipAiToolTests.cs (must pass unchanged)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs (ledger; must pass)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/data-mutation/RecordOwnership/ChatCreatedChildStampTests.cs (chat-created child carries I-1 stamp at create; route/chat/decision parity)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="016" status="required">Create and Repair modes complete in the service.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-008 (path A, spec ADR Tensions)">Scope: authorization. Route filters and `RequireAuthorization` on the child-records route stay exactly as they are. Payload-dependent checks run only in `CallerWriteAuthorization` via the service; do not copy them into the handlers or the route.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">Scope: error mapping. The route, chat handlers and decision cores use the ONE shared refusal map from task 013; the route's existing status codes and `errorCode` values for existing refusals do not change (NFR-07). Chat handlers keep their existing tool-error shape and take the code and text from the shared map.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: identity. Callers pass the caller principal (WhoAmI on the caller token inside the service). The handlers must not resolve WhoAmI separately and must not create with the user token. The create stays app-only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Scope: DI. Handlers take the already-registered scoped `RecordCreationService`; no new registration; no new interface.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-01 (spec)">Scope: every re-pointed caller. Fail closed: if the service throws or returns a refusal the caller reports a refusal and creates nothing through any fallback path; no caller may retain a direct-create fallback. Uniform 404 for "does not exist" and "cannot see" must be preserved on the route.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-08 / CLAUDE.md §8.5">Scope: coordination. UAC-r2 PR #2110 also edits OwnedChildWrite.cs, ChildRecordEndpoints.cs and CommunicationService.cs, and ontology-r1 owns the decision cores. Run /conflict-check FIRST (step 1); rebase on the PR if merged; do not edit CommunicationService.cs in this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: BFF publish. Placement Justification in the PR; fresh-master publish-size delta per §10.4; `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`; no package.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests added by this task. KEEP paths; no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;; no DI-registration tests. Cover the stated contract plus the named edge cases only. Existing suites change only where a deleted OwnedChildWrite create symbol was referenced, and only by re-pointing, never by weakening an assertion.</constraint>
  </constraints>

