  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`grep OwnedChildWrite.CreateAsync` in src/ returns nothing; `OwnedChildWrite` retains `RefileAsync` and no create entry point.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The child-records route, chat `dataverse.create_record`, `email.draft` and budget inquiry call `RecordCreationService` with the caller principal and no longer resolve WhoAmI themselves.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A chat-created child carries its I-1 stamp at create (asserted in the create payload / row), plus I-16 and the sharee mirror.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A parity test shows the route, chat and decision follow-on (`AddTodoExecutor`, `AssignWorkExecutor`) creates under the same parent produce the same owner and stamp.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The route's existing status codes and `errorCode` values for existing refusals are unchanged; route filters and the RouteAuthorizationGuardTests ledger are unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a caller who cannot AppendTo the parent gets the same uniform 404/403 on the route and the same refusal in chat as before; the service throwing or refusing creates nothing and no caller falls back to a direct create.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a chat create of a table that is not in RecordTableRules is refused (no create call).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF build 0 errors; SecureChildOwnershipAiToolTests*, RefileWriterAfterRefileGuardTests, RouteAuthorizationGuardTests, RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests and the decision (Signals) tests pass; publish-size delta, CVE result and /conflict-check result recorded in the task notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BLOCKING (ebilling-r1, 2026-10-21): do not re-point the child-record route or the chat create to RecordCreationService while master's OwnedChildWrite.CreateAsync carries the invoice-family guard (ebilling-r1 #1911) and RecordTableRules registers no invoice-family PreWriteRule for sprk_invoice and sprk_billingevent. The reconcile commit registers the rule and adds the 012-recipe test: every CoreRecordLookups key has an entry whose PreWriteRules contain the rule. It also retires the 013 ratchet baseline {sprk_invoice, sprk_billingevent}. It also adds:
      - F2: an additive PreWriteRefusal kind that maps invoice_family_read_failed and invoice_family_unknown_entity to Undecided 500, with PreWriteRefusal.NotFound() remaining the only path to the uniform 404;
      - F4: a test that a supersedes refusal keeps Code and Reason;
      - and it deletes one copy of the verbatim NotAvailableToFileUnder strings.
    Ask ebilling-r1 to review the reconcile commit.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">UAC-r2 review of 013 (2026-10-21).
      - Pre-create stamps: do not re-point a writer that stamps I-1/I-16 into the payload before the create (TaskActionCore.cs:229, TodoRegardingBuilder.cs:209, CommunicationService.cs:2532, DecisionRecordWriter.cs:1508) until the owner has decided the FR-06 step-10 amendment and the service implements it: pre-create derivation that refuses on failure, plus a post-create re-derivation; documents stay post-create.
      - K-4:
        - an upstream 401 now renders 403: decide and document it;
        - bodies carry correlationId, not traceId: check the clients;
        - remove the three existing membership publishes when re-pointing;
        - resolve the chat matter/project number change (OWNER/017).
      - SystemPrincipal: optionally narrow the 013 refusal. Let the plan run with an always-refuse callback mapped to 403, so ordinary parents proceed and secure parents are refused. An app-only AppendTo check on RequestedBy needs owner approval (ADR-028) and must fail closed on a null or unresolved RequestedBy.
      - Documents (whichever of this task and UAC-r2 #2169 lands second):
        - sprk_document.sprk_accessinheritance is refused for every principal (TableServerOwnedColumns on the document entry, plus the system path);
        - sprk_document.sprk_accesspermission is allowed for callers and refused for system principals, matching RefuseAppOnlyWrite.
        - Tests for each. UAC-r2 reviews.
      - Projects/matters caller-refused columns: owner decision before this task (#1608 related).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BLOCKING (DI-004 / #2188, 2026-10-21): before any caller is re-pointed, create-time mapping must not copy a source column the caller cannot read under field security. Read the source columns as the caller, or check field-security read per column. A denied column is dropped with a warning, timing-equalised and failing closed. Must-fire test: a field-secured source column the caller cannot read is not copied. Must-not-fire test: a readable column is copied. UAC-r2 reviews.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">From UAC-r2's re-check of 014 (2026-10-21):
      - R3-1: normalise ServerSetLookupColumns once (trimmed, case-insensitive) where the request is built, and have both the K-2/F-B guards and the existing AppendTo check read that normalised set. Test it.
      - R3-2: if it falls out naturally, move step 6's AppendTo for server-set root filing lookups (work assignment, project) to before step 3, so a refused create reads no mapping source. This is not a blocker; record the outcome.
    </criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">From UAC-r2's task 015 review (2026-10-21), blocking before any route reaches the unified create:
      - K1: a test where the catalog read in step 7 throws (`RetrieveMultipleAsync` faults) gets 503 `OwnerUnavailableCode` and nothing is written (RecordCreationService step 7, ~:609-630);
      - K3: a caller payload holding an explicit null under lowercase `sprk_ai_search_index@odata.bind` must not produce two keys that differ only in case after step 8's fill. Normalise the bind key (or drop the null entry before filling); test the duplicate-key case and the canonical-case case.
      Whichever of 017 or 018 lands first owns this; the other confirms it.
    </criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-13 part 1, FR-12, NFR-07, NFR-08. Office quick-create is task 018; widening the route to sprk_matter and sprk_project is task 020. Release note: chat-created children now get the I-1 stamp, I-16 and sharee mirror.</notes>

